  "notes": "{寝|ね}かせる is the transitive causative form of {寝|ね}る (to sleep). It is an ichidan verb ({一段動詞|いちだんどうし}).\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: Transitive ({他動詞|たどうし})\n- Pair: {寝|ね}る (intransitive — to sleep, to lie down)\n- Pattern: Xを{寝|ね}かせる\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {子|こ}どもを{寝|ね}かせる (to put the child to bed)\n- {生地|きじ}を{寝|ね}かせる (to let dough rest)\n- ワインを{寝|ね}かせる (to age wine)\n- {横|よこ}に{寝|ね}かせる (to lay on its side)\n\nUSAGE:\nSense 2 is widely used in cooking and food preparation. The idea is that letting something rest or age improves it, similar to English \"let it sit\" or \"let it age.\"",
